{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/4122","id":4118100690,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLKB0uM71dTrS","html_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4122","diff_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4122.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4122.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/issues/4122","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/4122/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/4122/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/issues/4122/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/statuses/6399803b660c34190bc08c4e437411fe401e2d20","number":4122,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(rtc): action keys ordering and chunking logic","user":{"login":"Maximellerbach","id":38923282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTIzMjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38923282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach","html_url":"https://github.com/Maximellerbach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Fixing some RTC related bugs\r\n\r\nduring rollouts I came across some weird behavior while using the rtc / async engine.\r\nhere are weird behavior / bug I found:\r\n\r\n- in some cases the joints wouldn't map correctly between sync vs rtc causing the arm to slam the table instead of going around it\r\n- by looking at the prediction graph, the seam of the predicted chunks were \"spiky\"\r\n- cold starts were quite agressive\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- enforced the actions to be re-ordered just like the sync engine does to avoid any disparity (this is the main fix).\r\n- aligned the rtc path to use the same `dataset_features` as the sync path (it was using `hw_features`).\r\n- fixed the padded actions to be \"hold\" instead of zero padded. (fixed the spiky chunk seam)\r\n- slighly changed how the latency is calculated on warmup\r\n\r\n## Related to\r\n- https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4223\r\n\r\n## How was this tested (or how to run locally)\r\n\r\nthis branch is composed of cherry picked commits from `experiments/wm-tshirt-folding`. Those changes were tested over there against the fastwam model.\r\n\r\nadded some unit tests for the padding and action keys ordering.","labels":[{"id":6829375825,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLKB0uM8AAAABlxABUQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/labels/policies","name":"policies","description":"Items related to robot policies","color":"6a737d","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6829388968,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLKB0uM8AAAABlxA0qA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/labels/tests","name":"tests","description":"Problems with test coverage, failures, or improvements to testing","color":"8dc149","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-23T16:05:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T17:05:04Z","closed_at":"2026-08-14T17:05:04Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":{"login":"Maximellerbach","i